---
title: Labneh
servings: 6
yield: 1 1/2 cups
tags: [middle eastern, vegetarian, make-ahead]
cuisine: middle eastern
time: 20 minutes, plus 12 to 24 hours straining
source: Labneh by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/labneh.html
---

Line a #colander{} with #cheesecloth{} and set it over a bowl, or plan to hang
the bundle from the tap or a spoon laid across a deep bowl.

Whisk the @plain yogurt{32%oz}(whole milk) with @salt{1%tsp} until even.

Scrape it onto the cloth and spread it out. Tie the corners into a knot and
let it drain ~{12%hours} to ~{24%hours}, on the counter or in the fridge. The
longer it drains, the thicker it gets.

Scrape the labneh off the cloth into a bowl and stir until smooth.

To serve, swirl it onto a plate and finish with @olive oil{} and whatever herbs
or spices you like.

> Strain up to 48 hours and it is firm enough to roll into balls and keep under
> olive oil for about a month. Plain labneh keeps two weeks in the fridge.
